  "claim_boundaries": [
    "This is a fully synthetic operating-characteristic calculation, not biological validation, expected assay power, or a wet-lab design selection.",
    "The raw-count bootstrap is a plug-in parametric test, not an exact randomization test or a constrained-likelihood calibration theorem.",
    "The guide channel is fixed at its generating value; calibration-sample uncertainty, batch drift, and model misspecification are not propagated.",
    "Wilson intervals quantify outer Monte Carlo binomial uncertainty only; they do not include inner-bootstrap or channel-calibration uncertainty.",
    "The population grouped-mean null retains nonzero guide-specific and culture-specific factorial interactions; a finite realized culture panel is not forced to have mean zero.",
    "The simulator has an independent implementation but uses the same correctly specified parametric observation model assumed by the estimator.",
    "The IID culture generator is one specified random-effects model and does not establish robustness to other heterogeneity distributions.",
    "The target-0 population mean association is deliberately large and synthetic, so its rejection rate is a sensitivity check rather than biological power.",
    "Smoke mode verifies execution and schema only; its four repetitions cannot assess error control or power."
